cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "quantifact: an investment-research agent that has to prove its numbers"
message: "If you use this software or its ideas, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Leon
    website: "https://github.com/leoncuhk"
repository-code: "https://github.com/leoncuhk/quantifact"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.3.0a1
date-released: 2026-08-13
keywords:
  - llm agents
  - investment research
  - point-in-time
  - data contracts
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  quantifact treats agentic analysis as a compiler problem: a question is
  clarified into an intermediate representation with schemas, units, row grain
  and a knowledge date; each task compiles in parallel into one pandas function;
  static analysis derives the dependency graph; layered contracts run as
  ordinary Python; and a caching harness executes the code bound to the
  knowledge date, making look-ahead structurally impossible rather than
  discouraged.
